{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויבא הפליט", :translit "va'yavo ha'palit", :gloss "and the fugitive came"} {:he "בא אלי הפליט מירושלים לאמר הוכתה העיר", :translit "ba elai ha'palit mi'yerushalayim leimor hukatah ha'ir", :gloss "the fugitive came to me from Jerusalem saying: the city has been struck"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word 'הפליט' (the fugitive) linked across verses via shared root and midrashic theme of escape from falling"}], :frame {:text "Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer identifies the fugitive of Genesis 14:13 with an angelic episode: when the Holy One cast Samael down, Samael grabbed Michael's wings to pull him down too, but God rescued Michael (Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer, chapter on the war of the kings). The Ba'al HaTurim then draws a verbal link to Ezekiel 33:21, where 'the fugitive came to me from Jerusalem, saying: the city has been struck,' showing the word הפליט used for one who escapes catastrophe.", :sources ["Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer" "Ezekiel 33:21"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word 'הפליט' (the fugitive) linked across verses via shared root and midrashic theme of escape from falling", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:05:47.103014636Z", :model "glm-5.2"}